{"id":"b83d63897d58e956","group":"58","path":"58/batch20/58-df-hurewicz.md","title":"Hurewicz Theorem","display":"df-hurewicz — Hurewicz Theorem","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-hurewicz","aliases":["58-df-hurewicz"],"display":"df-hurewicz — Hurewicz Theorem","depends_on":["[[58-df-hurewicz-map]]","[[58-df-bijective]]","[[58-df-path-connected]]","[[58-df-equinumerous]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-hurewicz"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-hurewicz</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-hurewicz — Hurewicz Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"4b65b240558a9358\" href=\"?note=4b65b240558a9358\" title=\"58-df-hurewicz-map\">58-df-hurewicz-map</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"d583890235faf0d5\" href=\"?note=d583890235faf0d5\" title=\"58-df-bijective\">58-df-bijective</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"c100dce18000d9e7\" href=\"?note=c100dce18000d9e7\" title=\"58-df-path-connected\">58-df-path-connected</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"28c79fde9f892bfe\" href=\"?note=28c79fde9f892bfe\" title=\"58-df-equinumerous\">58-df-equinumerous</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,\\tau,x_0,h_k\\in V\">\\(X,\\tau,x_0,h_k\\in V\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}\">\\(k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}\\)</span></li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)\">\\(\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c100dce18000d9e7\" href=\"?note=c100dce18000d9e7\" title=\"58-df-path-connected\">58-df-path-connected</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,x_0,k)\">\\(\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,x_0,k)\\)</span> (see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"4b65b240558a9358\" href=\"?note=4b65b240558a9358\" title=\"58-df-hurewicz-map\">58-df-hurewicz-map</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Bijective}\">\\(\\mathrm{Bijective}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S\\)</span> (bijection and equinumerosity predicates)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hurewicz}\\vdash\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)\\land x_0\\in X\\land k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}\\land\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,\\tau,x_0,k)\\land\\forall i\\in k\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(\\pi_i(X,x_0),1)\\Bigr)\\to\\mathrm{Bijective}\\bigl(h_k,\\pi_k(X,x_0),H_k(X;\\mathbb Z)\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hurewicz}\\vdash\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)\\land x_0\\in X\\land k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}\\land\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,\\tau,x_0,k)\\land\\forall i\\in k\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(\\pi_i(X,x_0),1)\\Bigr)\\to\\mathrm{Bijective}\\bigl(h_k,\\pi_k(X,x_0),H_k(X;\\mathbb Z)\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The topology argument required by the five-place Hurewicz-map predicate is explicit, and triviality uses the registered equinumerosity predicate.</li>\n<li>Relative Hurewicz theorem relates <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\pi_n(X,A)\">\\(\\pi_n(X,A)\\)</span> to <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"H_n(X,A)\">\\(H_n(X,A)\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Homological algebra analog: Tor measures deviation from exactness.</li>\n<li>Hurewicz is first non-vanishing stage for homology.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"58-df-hurewicz-map","status":"resolved","id":"4b65b240558a9358","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-hurewicz-map]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-bijective","status":"resolved","id":"d583890235faf0d5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-bijective]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-path-connected","status":"resolved","id":"c100dce18000d9e7","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-path-connected]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-equinumerous","status":"resolved","id":"28c79fde9f892bfe","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[58-df-equinumerous]]","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-path-connected","status":"resolved","id":"c100dce18000d9e7","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)$ (see [[58-df-path-connected]])","embed":false},{"target":"58-df-hurewicz-map","status":"resolved","id":"4b65b240558a9358","anchor":"ref-6","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,x_0,k)$ (see [[58-df-hurewicz-map]])","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,\\tau,x_0,h_k\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,x_0,k)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Bijective}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}hurewicz}\\vdash\\Bigl(\\operatorname{PathConnected}_S(X,\\tau)\\land x_0\\in X\\land k\\in\\omega\\setminus\\{0,1\\}\\land\\mathrm{HurewiczMap}_S(h_k,X,\\tau,x_0,k)\\land\\forall i\\in k\\setminus\\{0\\}\\;\\mathrm{Equinumerous}_S(\\pi_i(X,x_0),1)\\Bigr)\\to\\mathrm{Bijective}\\bigl(h_k,\\pi_k(X,x_0),H_k(X;\\mathbb Z)\\bigr)","display":true},{"tex":"\\pi_n(X,A)","display":false},{"tex":"H_n(X,A)","display":false}],"bytes":1314,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-652","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch20/58-df-hurewicz.md|58-df-hurewicz]]（batch20）"}],"outgoing":["4b65b240558a9358","d583890235faf0d5","c100dce18000d9e7","28c79fde9f892bfe"]}